1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,260
Reading Task

2
00:00:04,320 --> 00:00:07,120
An Early Farmer Pioneer

3
00:00:09,240 --> 00:00:12,540
Some people thought Jia Sixie was a lucky man.

4
00:00:13,100 --> 00:00:15,980
He had worked for the emperor and when he got old,

5
00:00:15,980 --> 00:00:18,780
he was able to go to his hometown to relax.

6
00:00:19,720 --> 00:00:22,320
Jia Sixie, however, had other plans.

7
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:29,720
He had always been interested in agriculture and intended to do something to make Chinese farming even better.

8
00:00:34,480 --> 00:00:38,600
He was born in Yidu in Shandong Province and worked in Gaoyang,

9
00:00:38,820 --> 00:00:40,160
which is also in Shandong.

10
00:00:41,240 --> 00:00:46,420
As he rode through the countryside on his journeys for his work he looked out at the fields.

11
00:00:47,380 --> 00:00:50,540
Some of them were greener and had more crops than others.

12
00:00:51,300 --> 00:00:54,360
Some cows and sheep looked healthier than others too.

13
00:00:55,100 --> 00:00:56,860
He was lost in thought.

14
00:00:57,680 --> 00:01:01,560
What could a farmer do to get good crops from his fields?

15
00:01:02,600 --> 00:01:04,960
Surely there must be rules that would help them.

16
00:01:06,160 --> 00:01:09,600
He thought he could use his knowledge to find out the best ways

17
00:01:09,600 --> 00:01:13,140
for farmers to grow crops and then write a book to help them.

18
00:01:14,200 --> 00:01:18,780
In doing so he collected information from farmers who did well,

19
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:22,240
studied it and did experiments to find the best way.

20
00:01:31,920 --> 00:01:35,080
Then he told them to hang them up to dry all winter.

21
00:01:36,120 --> 00:01:39,560
The next spring the seeds should be knocked out of their seed-heads

22
00:01:39,560 --> 00:01:40,180
and planted.

23
00:01:41,380 --> 00:01:43,460
He studied how to improve the soil.

24
00:01:44,240 --> 00:01:48,660
He advised farmers to clear weeds from the ground before planting crops.

25
00:01:49,400 --> 00:01:53,480
They could either let the animals eat the weeds or turn the soil over

26
00:01:53,480 --> 00:01:55,760
so that the weeds were covered and would rot.

27
00:01:56,880 --> 00:01:59,380
Then he gave advice on turning over the soil.

28
00:02:00,620 --> 00:02:03,840
The first time each year, farmers should dig deeply,

29
00:02:03,940 --> 00:02:06,680
but the second time should be less deep.

30
00:02:13,340 --> 00:02:17,240
He suggested changing crops in the field every year:

31
00:02:17,760 --> 00:02:22,160
rice one year and wheat the next so that they would always get good harvests.

32
00:02:23,080 --> 00:02:27,020
They should also grow different plants next to each other in the field.

33
00:02:27,600 --> 00:02:30,040
He also gave advice on how to fish,

34
00:02:30,100 --> 00:02:32,460
keep a garden and even make wine.

35
00:02:42,960 --> 00:02:45,400
For centuries after Jia Sixie died,

36
00:02:45,760 --> 00:02:49,020
it was studied by Chinese farmers and students of agriculture.
